-- title:
--   Regularity of C[J/varpiₜ] at places where j is regular
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\ne q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. The hypothesis `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, pinned by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, $K$ is generated over $L$, inside $L((X))$, by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb Q\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ with $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The ring $A$ is a domain which is a discrete valuation ring and a henselian local ring, equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field; $q$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A\to L$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero and its Laurent expansion is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image in $L((X))$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Further, $\varpi\in A$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $j$-chart algebra, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-chart and of the $j^{-1}$-chart along the middle chart. The ideal $y\subseteq C$ is maximal (`hy`), contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart hypothesis `hArig` (seven clauses, summarised here).** For every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism $\mathfrak X\to\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y')=z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` with $y'$ in place of $y$, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v-fu\bigr)$, such that: (1) $e$ takes the germ of the image of $a\in A$ to the class of the constant $\sigma a$; (2) every $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ realising, in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), the modular substitution attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserves $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, such a $\tau$ acts trivially on $C/y'$; (4) any such $\tau$ (for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) preserving $C$ and acting trivially on $C/y'$ is realised on $S$ by a ring automorphism $\theta$ compatible with $\tau$ through $e$ and the germ map, fixing the constants, and acting on the tangent directions by a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$, with $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (5) two prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each failing to contain one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of the constant $\sigma\varpi$, and each containing an element congruent to $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with integers satisfying $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk along $e$; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ not containing one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, and containing an element congruent to $X_0$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to the image of some $a_0\in A$, and the difference has $e$-image the class of some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ leading form $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}h\cdot a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **The fixed point and the fixed chart witness.** A point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ is fixed, together with $\varpi_z$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) and lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`); a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y')=z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$ (`hy'y`). Further fixed are a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1-f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW_1` asserts for this witness exactly the conjunction of the seven clauses just described.
--
--   **The centre, the blown-up chart and the valuation ring.** The ideal $J\subseteq C$ is pinned by `hJ` to be the infimum of the ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\bigl(\text{contraction along } e_1\circ(\text{completion})\circ(\text{germ at }z)\text{ of }(\sigma_1\varpi_t,X_0,X_1)S\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ realising $\gamma^{-1}$ as above and preserving $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is pinned by `hB` to be the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra, that is $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. Finally $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ with $B\subseteq W$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses are: `hR1`, that $C\le B$ and every $f\in K$ satisfies $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $h\ne 0$; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), namely (a) for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) whose kernel consists of the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to k\to\mathrm{CoordRing}$, and such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ realising $\gamma^{-1}$ and stabilising $W$ there is $c\in\mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\gamma\bmod q,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,c)\mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$) intertwining $\rho\circ\tau$ with `hAction` of that pair, and with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (b) the automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; (c) every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ arises from some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ realising $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense that every $b\in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ has $\tau b\in B$ and $\tau b\in Q$; (d) if $b\in B$ satisfies $\tau b\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ realising $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau b\in B$, then the image of $\varpi$ divides $b$ in $B$; (e) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ realising $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ (that is, $b\in y\iff \tau b\in y$ for $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$), then $W$ is $\tau$-stable, $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Every $f\in K$ belonging to $B$ satisfies: for every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ — a valuation subring of $K$, different from $K$, containing the image of $L$ and being a principal ideal ring — if $\operatorname{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$ then $\operatorname{ord}_P(f)\ge 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_P$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb Z^{m0}$-valued adic valuation.
--
--   This is the regularity half of the analysis of the blown-up chart $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$ attached to a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$: functions in $B$ have no poles at any place of $K/L$ at which $j$ itself is regular, so all their poles are concentrated at the cusps. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked) in the construction of an end-adapted chart of finite type.
